From 750e02fbf87652aea37000d20cb27805f1a85417 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Poncho <poncho@spahan.ch>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 11:22:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fit: Restore hp_ngl to include MTP layers in GPU offload
 budget
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Commit 9a688e51e changed hp_ngl to exclude MTP layers when load_mtp is
false, intending to avoid allocating memory for unused tensors. However
hp_ngl is not a memory budget — it is the assertion bound for
n_gpu_layers and determines how many layers the fitter can assign to GPU.

Reducing hp_ngl by n_layer_nextn capped assignable layers from 42 to 41,
forcing layer 0 onto CPU and causing ~28% throughput regression on MoE
models with MTP (e.g. Qwen3.5-A3B). Tensor skipping for unloaded MTP
layers is handled independently by TENSOR_SKIP in llama-model.cpp.

Restore the original calculation: hp_ngl = n_layer + n_layer_nextn.
---
 common/fit.cpp | 5 +----
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/common/fit.cpp b/common/fit.cpp
index dd1f3ef76..c82d066ad 100644
--- a/common/fit.cpp
+++ b/common/fit.cpp
@@ -136,10 +136,7 @@ static std::vector<llama_device_memory_data> common_get_device_memory_data_impl(
         devs.push_back(llama_model_get_device(model, i));
     }
 
-    hp_ngl         = llama_model_n_layer(model);
-    if (mparams->load_mtp) {
-        hp_ngl    += llama_model_n_layer_nextn(model);
-    }
+    hp_ngl         = llama_model_n_layer(model) + llama_model_n_layer_nextn(model);
     hp_n_ctx_train = llama_model_n_ctx_train(model);
     hp_n_expert    = llama_model_n_expert(model);
 
